{{also|Bodega|bodegă}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|es|bodega}}, from {{der|en|la|apotheca||storehouse}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀποθήκη||storehouse}}. {{doublet|en|boutique}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/boʊˈdeɪɡə/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-bodega.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A storehouse for maturing wine, a [[winery]].
# A store specializing in [[Hispanic]] groceries.
# {{lb|en|slang|New York City}} Any [[convenience store]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=[[w:N. K. Jemisin|N. K. Jemisin]]|title=[[w:The City We Became|The City We Became]]|publisher=Orbit|page=83|passage=He [...] finds himself looking across the street, at a little '''bodega''' on the corner.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|Southwestern United States}} Any small or medium sized shop with a unique facade in a shopping center plaza, usually located in the center or the sides of the plaza. Does not include the {{w|anchor tenant}} of the shopping center, as they are usually referred to as the [[anchor]].
# {{lb|en|Philippines}} A [[warehouse]].

====See also====
* {{l|en|apothecary}}
* {{l|en|boutique}}

